      "writtenOn": "2021-06-16T22:01:18Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yeah. This is the other side of the issue.\n\nIn both case (either high power or idle), isEnabledForSystem should be involved in the consolidation fo the thresholds.  Only when it is true firstly then we start to consider if system threshold should be honored (true in two cases, high power or app explicitly request in idle).\n\nFor example, when RSRNR is disabled for EUTRAN, then the consolidatedThresholds should not take system threshold of RSRNR at all.\n\nNow in idle mode, system threshold are consolidated only when all condition are true:\n1. isEnabledForSystem is true AND\n2. Device is in hight power mode OR in idle mode but app explicitly request to report system thresholds",
      "parentUuid": "31d44ca9_5e5e0548",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 4047,
        "startChar": 74,
        "endLine": 4047,
        "endChar": 92
